/* The input language reserves the terminal br for nondeterministic choice:
   br a b stands for the outputs a and b, and the specification must hold of
   both.  q0 accepts a but not b, so the output b violates it: unsat.  The
   program is linear and has no coercion, but it writes br, for which the
   reduction's completeness is not established, so the refutation is
   reported only because running the program confirms it. */
%BEGING
Main -> br a b.
%ENDG
%BEGINA
q0 a -> .
q1 b -> .
%ENDA
%BEGINT
Main : q0.
%ENDT
